        "timestamp": 1774558892,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Return hubs' for migrants clear EU parliament hurdle Europe Issued on: 26/03/2026 - 22:01 European lawmakers cleared the way Thursday for tougher penalties for irregular migrants and their potential deportation to so-called \"return hubs\" outside the bloc. The measures, criticised by human rights groups, are part of a tightening of Europe's immigration rules in response to pressure across the 27-nation bloc to curb migration. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports. Russia's spring offensive in Ukraine expected to focus on 'Fortress Belt' in Donetsk region 26/03/2026 Europe Georgia’s links to Iran: Ex-Defense Minister Khidasheli denounces Al-Mustafa University activities 25/03/2026 Europe Ex-EU border chief faces French investigation for crimes against humanity 25/03/2026 Europe Denmark faces tough coalition talks following election 25/03/2026 Europe Cancer nurse turned archbishop installed as first female Church of England leader 25/03/2026 Europe Ukrainian drones crash in Estonia and Latvia, raising air defence concerns 25/03/2026 Europe Ghana and EU sign defence partnership to counter west Africa insecurity 25/03/2026 Africa Ukraine: Massive wave of daytime Russian strikes hits sites nationwide 25/03/2026 Europe Danish election signals shift toward Dutch and Belgian-style of coalition building 25/03/2026 Europe"
