        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russia's spring offensive in Ukraine expected to focus on 'Fortress Belt' in Donetsk region Europe Issued on: 26/03/2026 - 21:50 Russia's spring offensive in Ukraine is expected to focus on the so-called \"Fortress Belt\" ​of heavily defended cities in Ukraine's eastern Donetsk region, which Moscow has repeatedly demanded Kyiv relinquish in return for peace. Speaking on FRANCE 24, retired Vice Admiral of the US Navy Robert B Murrett, says that the region is \"a veritable highway for any army that wanted to conduct operations further into Ukraine and beyond\". Georgia’s links to Iran: Ex-Defense Minister Khidasheli denounces Al-Mustafa University activities 25/03/2026 Europe Ex-EU border chief faces French investigation for crimes against humanity 25/03/2026 Europe Denmark faces tough coalition talks following election 25/03/2026 Europe Cancer nurse turned archbishop installed as first female Church of England leader 25/03/2026 Europe Ukrainian drones crash in Estonia and Latvia, raising air defence concerns 25/03/2026 Europe Ghana and EU sign defence partnership to counter west Africa insecurity 25/03/2026 Africa Ukraine: Massive wave of daytime Russian strikes hits sites nationwide 25/03/2026 Europe Danish election signals shift toward Dutch and Belgian-style of coalition building 25/03/2026 Europe Danish PM hands in government resignation after defeat in general election 25/03/2026 Europe"
